<title>SWITZERLAND: EMS Chemie details share buyback results.</title>
<headline>EMS Chemie details share buyback results.</headline>
<dateline>ZURICH 1997-03-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>EMS-Chemie Holding AG said it had been offered 69,361 bearer shares under its March 14 offer to buy back up to 40,000 shares at 6,000 Swiss francs each.</p>
<p>&quot;This very good result leads to a proportional allocation rate of 57.67 percent,&quot; it said in a statement.</p>
<p>If shareholders approve, the company's share capital will thus be reduced by two million francs to 28 million, divided into 414,140 bearer shares of 50 francs par and 729,300 registered shares at 10 francs par, it said.</p>
<p>EMS shares were down 160 at 5,910 at 1415 GMT.</p>
<p>-- Zurich newsroom +41 1 631 7340</p>
</text>
